  "caption": "Quinn bought full lycra, borrowed a bike, guessed the setup and rode 60 km on day one. Next morning, the knees filed a formal complaint.\n\nCycling knee pain is common and often very fixable. Thousands of pedal strokes an hour magnify small bike-fit errors, especially with a sudden jump in distance.\n\nWhat can help: set saddle height so the knee is moderately bent at the bottom of the stroke, check saddle fore-aft position and cleat alignment, spin lighter gears at a higher cadence, build distance gradually, and add single-leg strength work. Knee pain doesn't automatically mean you must stop riding.\n\nGet it checked if pain persists, the knee swells or catches, or nothing changes after a few weeks.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
